  "reason": "The occurrence 'essential proteins' is defined broadly as 'proteins requiring active intracellular transport'. The existing concept 'motor proteins' is defined specifically as 'proteins that move along microtubules to transport essential proteins'. While motor proteins are the agents of this transport, they are distinct entities from the cargo (essential proteins) they carry. The occurrence refers to the cargo class, whereas the existing concept refers to the transporter class. They represent different biological roles and identities, not synonyms or aliases."
